From 6f451c30f74256be61f60502ba0e9b71eacb67fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 04:03:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02250/11362] [outer-loop] ARC loop iter 2 + budget-realism:
 8/11 games solve from scratch (was 'gaps')

Iter 2: HUD-masking capability in StepwiseExplorer (hud_mask=) -- measured WASH (neutral
on levels, probe costs competition actions), kept opt-in/off-by-default.
BIG FINDING: the 6000-action eval budget badly understated solve-rate. At 20000 actions
the explorer solves 8/11 public games from scratch (r11l/ls20/cd82/su15/tu93 close at
8-11k) -- those were BUDGET-limited, not mechanic-limited (competition allows ~96k/game).
Default budget 6000->20000. True scorecard: 8 levels, 3 gaps.
The 3 genuinely-hard (wa30/cn04/sk48) resist 45k: the BATCH solver gets cn04/sk48 in ~12k
EXPANSIONS but step-wise pays nav cost PER STATE -> unreachable by action-count. They need
E3 (plan in a model = few actions), which is also the EFFICIENCY lever (the 8 solves score
~0 efficiency). E3 is the next loop lever, not more explorer tweaks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
